//! The `mask-type` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property applies to the
//! SVG `mask` element. It defines whether to use the _luminance_ (brightness) or _alpha_
//! (transparency) content of the mask. This property may be overridden by the `mask-mode` property.
//! The `mask-type` property has no effect on image or gradient masks.
//!
//! Initial: luminance. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Grammar: luminance | alpha
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-masking-1/#propdef-mask-type
//!
//! Author guide: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/mask-type
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

module std.css.properties.MaskType.

